  "title": "The knot's contradiction is a balance of spin sectors, and its amplitude is not spin-local",
  "subject": "The spin-structure decomposition of the knot's colouring counts on the surfaces of its three-fold spaces",
  "conclusion": "The knot's colouring counts are Arf-signed averages of spin sectors, so its non-colourability is an exact balance of even and odd sectors (8, 8, 8 against 24 on the Fano torus), and its sign class is the only non-colourable one among the surface's Kasteleyn classes. Opening a contact gives 16, 16, 16 and 28, so five per handle does not come from the even spin structures, and at genus 2 the sectors do not factor over handles.",
